Part 5 - Training and Testing Data

I would divide the dataset into 80% training data and 20% testing data.
Training Data: 80% — about 3,415 loan applications
Testing Data: 20% — about 854 loan applications

The training data is used to teach the Logistic Regression model and help it find patterns between the applicant information and whether the
loan was approved or rejected.

It is important to keep the testing data separate because the model should be tested on data that it has not seen before. If I tested the
model using the same data it was trained on, the results could make the model look more accurate than it actually is. Using separate testing
data gives me a better idea of how well the model would perform on new loan applications.

I chose an 80/20 split because it gives the model plenty of data to learn from while still having enough data to accurately test its 
performance.
